drm/msm/dpu: one DSC encoder for single-slice panels

With DSC the encoder takes two DSC encoders (and two mixers) whenever the
SoC has two, merged on one interface. That splits each line between the
encoders and needs at least two slices per line. The Xiaomi 12 panel
(l3-42-02-0a) has one 1080-wide slice, stock uses topology 1:1:1: with two
encoders the DSI got a different byte count per line, the command-mode
transfer never finished (pp_done timeouts, DCS commands then -110) and the
panel showed the first lines followed by garbage (seen on 6.17). Use two
encoders on one interface only for configs with at least two slices.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index 1f20695f8..567147568 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -686,7 +686,14 @@ void dpu_encoder_update_topology(struct drm_encoder *drm_enc,
 		 */
 		WARN(topology->num_intf > 2,
 		     "DSC topology cannot support more than 2 interfaces\n");
-		if (topology->num_intf >= 2 || dpu_kms->catalog->dsc_count >= 2)
+		/*
+		 * Two DSC encoders on one interface are merged and split each
+		 * line between them, which needs at least two slices per line.
+		 * A single-slice panel (Xiaomi 12: one 1080-wide slice, stock
+		 * topology 1:1:1) gets garbage and every frame times out.
+		 */
+		if (topology->num_intf >= 2 ||
+		    (dpu_kms->catalog->dsc_count >= 2 && dsc->slice_count >= 2))
 			topology->num_dsc = 2;
 		else
 			topology->num_dsc = 1;
